---
interface Props {greeting?:boolean}
const {greeting=false}=Astro.props;
---
<figure class="teaching-example">
 <div><p>Pseudocode</p><pre><code>{greeting?'ASK "What is your name? " INTO name\nSHOW "Hello, ", name':'SHOW "Hello"'}</code></pre></div>
 <div><p>Output</p><pre><samp>{greeting?'What is your name? Sam\nHello, Sam':'Hello'}</samp></pre></div>
 <figcaption>{greeting?'Where you’re headed: a program that asks for a name and greets its player. From Asking the Player, Unit 5. Pseudocode describes the idea.':'From The Basics: A Program Is Instructions. This static example shows how the pseudocode produces its result, independently of a language.'}</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
.teaching-example{width:100%;min-width:0;margin:0}.teaching-example>div{padding:24px;background:var(--h-ground);border-top:1px solid var(--h-line)}
.teaching-example p{font:1rem/1.5 var(--h-font-ui);margin:0 0 16px;color:var(--h-ink-muted)}.teaching-example pre{margin:0;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:none;padding:0}
.teaching-example :is(code,samp){font:1rem/1.6 var(--h-font-mono);color:var(--h-spot-ink)}.teaching-example figcaption{width:100%;font:italic .875rem/1.5 var(--h-font-ui);margin-top:12px;color:var(--h-ink-muted)}
</style>
